Subject: [PATCH] linux-firmware: qcom: nord: rebuild NORD-RIDE topology with
 the playback fix

The NORD-RIDE topology from the v1.0.5 sync is built from an
audioreach-topology tree whose nord-ride playback device graph is missing
a comma, so the graph values end up misconfigured and playback fails on
the Nord RIDE board.

Rebuild NORD-RIDE-tplg.bin from audioreach-topology 44110d19, which is the
same v1.0.5 content plus that fix.

Link: https://github.com/linux-msm/audioreach-topology/pull/93
Signed-off-by: Mohammad Rafi Shaik <mohammad.rafi.shaik@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending [fix merged in audioreach-topology as 44110d19; waiting for the next linux-firmware sync]
---
 qcom/nord/NORD-RIDE-tplg.bin | Bin 11116 -> 11116 bytes
 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

